course: dictionary
lesson: 705
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word bar is a good example. «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars» means the metal rods of a cage, not a drink counter, because the animals are kept safe behind them.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In «If a bar left in a hot car melts and sets again», the bar is a chocolate bar, because things that melt are usually food like chocolate. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then try it and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Music has its own meaning too. «In 3/4 time each bar holds three crotchet beats» shows that a bar is a short part of a tune with a set number of beats. Here bar means a unit of time in music, not a piece of metal or chocolate.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Bar can be a noun for a thing: a bar of soap, a chocolate bar, or the bars of a cage.
fact: Bar can also be a verb, which means to block or forbid.
fact: A bar graph uses bars to show numbers, and a bar can also be a place or counter where drinks or food are served.
fact: In music, a bar is a short part with a set number of beats.
exercise: «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars.» What are bars in this sentence? | *Metal rods that keep animals in | A graph with numbers | Long, solid pieces of chocolate | A place where drinks are served
exercise: «If a bar left in a hot car melts and sets again, it turns grey and crumbly.» What kind of bar is this? | A bar graph | A bar of metal | *A chocolate bar | A music bar
exercise: «In 3/4 time each bar holds three crotchet beats.» What is a bar in this sentence? | A long rod of wood | A graph with numbers | A place to buy drinks | *A short part of music with a set number of beats
test: A bar graph uses what to show numbers? | *Bars | Pictures of animals | Words only | Colours only
test: «The workers barred the gate at night.» What does barred mean here? | Painted | *Blocked, so nobody could get in | Opened wide | Counted
exam: Which sentence uses bar to mean a place where drinks are served? | The bar of soap was soft and white | *The bar was busy, with people ordering drinks at the counter | The bar graph showed the sales for each month | The bar on the cage was cold
